target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestDroppedGatesCollapsesEveryFalsyStatus'
expect: a falsy status must not reach the caller verbatim
why:    the Python stores `st or "unreported"`, so EVERY falsy status collapses to "unreported" — not only an absent entry but also "", 0 and false. Defaulting only on absence reported "", "0" and "false" to the caller: a parity break, and an alarm line that names nothing where the status is the only thing naming the gate's problem. Not hypothetical — the status vocabulary is open because cmd_finish never validates the string, and a non-string status reaching this path has already happened once.
--- old
		if !truthy(raw) {
			status = "unreported"
		}
--- new
		if raw == nil {
			status = "unreported"
		}
